item.content:encoded:
I asked my daughter, &ldquo;What was the theme for the class?&rdquo;


...When I asked her what her thoughts or inspirations were for her design, she said &ldquo;Maybe, &hellip; BBQ?&rdquo;


I have never been one to pretend to understand the complexities or themes behind art, but I know what I like and don&rsquo;t like.    Looking at my daughter&rsquo;s flower/vegetable arrangement, I have no real idea how she came up with what you see, but I like the balance and colour, and in the end, isn&rsquo;t that all that matters?


So for all you out there with odds and ends leftover in your garden, or in your fridge, use my daughter&rsquo;s arrangement to give you inspiration.

I didn&rsquo;t have one every day, or even every week, but I ate quite a lot of them over my time in high school.


...I usually don&rsquo;t put nuts in cinnamon buns, but we&rsquo;ve had some nuts around for a while so I thought, &ldquo;Hey, why not put them in?&rdquo;


The buns were finished baking just before dinner time and after dinner I just had to have a small taste.  ...  Well if you don&rsquo;t like these things, these buns aren&rsquo;t for you.    And if you do like these things, well, again (sorry) these buns aren&rsquo;t for you.
